{
  "note": "🪟️ One language-neutral contract for the question BOTH renderer targets have to answer the same way: given an app manifest and an active mode, which window INSTANCES are laid out, in what tree, at what fractions, and which one is focused. React answers it with `resolveLayoutForMode` (🎠️kernel/🟦️.ts) + `resolveFrameworkLayoutSeed`/`collectFrameworkLayoutWindowSeeds` (🛠️ShellHelpers/🟦️.tsx); wgpu answers it with `semio_framework::resolve_layout_for_mode` + `DockState::from_app`/`apply_layout_diff` (🛰️Dock/🎯️targets/🧊️wgpu/🦀️.rs) and then SOLVES the tree into rects the chrome walk paints. Before this fixture existed the wgpu shell painted `active_window_id` alone over the whole body and never consulted the dock at all, so edit mode's Preview window had no rect, no arena subtree and no World3d engine surface (ticket 26/09/09/PROCEDURAL-3D-END-TO-END).",
  "provenance": {
    "generation3d-edit": "✏️s/🔌️plugins/🌀️procedural/🗿️artifacts/🧊️generation3d/🏅️standards/🔖️1/🪆️subsets/✳️any/✏️editor/🎭️modes/✏️edit/🦀️.rs — `create_default_layout([flow, preview], \"row\", [68.0, 32.0], [\"Flow\", \"Preview\"])`, mode `edit` with no `layout_id`, so the app's `default_layout`.",
    "generation3d-generate": "…/✏️editor/🎭️modes/🧬️generate/🦀️.rs — named layout `generation3d-generate`, `create_default_layout([generations, form, preview], \"row\", [22.0, 43.0, 35.0], …)`, referenced by mode `generate`'s `layout_id`.",
    "generation3d-view": "…/👁️viewer/🎭️modes/👁️view/🦀️.rs — a single full-pane stack with one window.",
    "canvasNote": "`canvas` is the dock canvas the wgpu chrome walk hands the root (the body rect inset by the theme's panel inset). React lays the same tree out with CSS flex and is asserted on the TREE and the FRACTIONS, not on pixels; the Rust law additionally solves the tree with the dock's own solver and asserts these rects."
  },
